Differential expression analysis was performed using DESeq2
(v1.44.0).

Translation efficiency was estimated using an interaction model:

~ condition + seqType + condition:seqType

where:
condition = Control or Treatment
seqType = RNA or RPF

The interaction term represents TE changes:
"conditionTreat.seqTypeRPF"

Algorithem:
The interaction coefficient is:

*** [log_2(RPF/RNA)_Treat] - [log_2(RPF/RNA)_Ctrl] ***

which is:

*** log_2 (RPF_Treat/RNA_Treat} / RPF_Ctrl/RNA_Ctrl) ***

Therefore:

*** log2FC_interaction = log2(Treat_TE/Ctrl_TE) ***

Note: the DESeq2 calculation for interaction coefficient is not exactly the value of log2(Treat_TE) - log2(Ctrl_TE)
Reason: it is the GLM-estimated TE fold change, not necessarily the exact arithmetic value obtained from directly calculating TE ratios from group means;
        While for genes with decent counts and stable replicates, the two are often extremely close
